[run1_hdc_degradation]
An attempted direct `hdc hilog -r` was interpreted as a continuous HiLog stream and was terminated by timeout before the scripted Ability start ran. A retry using guest shell commands did not return: hilog clear timed out at 2026-07-17T00:59:39+08:00 and the subsequent aa start timed out without a success response. At 2026-07-17T01:01:08+08:00, list targets still showed Connected but `timeout 20 hdc ... shell echo diagnostic-smoke` exited 124. This was recorded as an HDC shell RPC failure and not hidden by target status. Kernel logs concurrently contained watchdog_service restarts and `teleport_express release when wait ... timeout`; they are accompanying observations, not a proven cause.
